[[File:Venator slayer icon.png|left]]
'''Venators''' are [[Slayer monster]]s that require 74 [[Slayer]] and completion of the quest [[The Blood Moon Rises]] to fight. Compared to [[vyrewatch sentinel]]s, they are a higher-intensity encounter with a better drop rate for [[blood shard]]s, along with a relatively decent supply of [[dragon arrowtips]] and [[dragon dart tip]]s via their [[venator fang|fang]] and [[venator tooth|teeth]] drops. Like vyrewatch sentinels, they are considered [[Vampyre (attribute)#Tier 3 Vampyres|tier 3 vampyres]] and can only be killed with specific [[vampyrebane weapons]]. If the ''[[Bigger and Badder]]'' Slayer reward is unlocked, there is a chance for a [[blood-starved venator]] to spawn upon killing a venator, even when off-task.

Players may only attack venators on-task if they have been assigned [[vampyre]]s from their corresponding slayer master, or a venator task if assigned from [[Mortimer]]. Players may also kill venators off-task by paying the nearby aranei with [[Stymphike feather]]s; each off-task kill requires 30 feathers, costing a total of {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Stymphike feather|30}}}} coins.

Venators will attack with melee if next to the player, or ranged otherwise. Praying correctly will negate all ranged damage and most melee damage. Whenever a venator damages a player with melee, it will heal the same amount. Occasionally, a venator will charge up a shriek attack. If the player has a [[Protection prayers|protection prayer]] active during the shriek, they will see the message {{Mes|The venator's screech disrupts your concentration!|colour=red}}, taking damage and losing some prayer points. This will hit once every tick for the duration of the screech. When wearing [[earmuffs]] or a [[Slayer helmet]], the damage from the shriek is significantly reduced and it ends one tick sooner.

If killed with a [[Sunspear]] special attack, they will additionally add a [[venator heart]] directly to the player's inventory if they have free space, displaying the message {{Mes|Your spear pierces the venator's heart and rips it free.|colour=red}}. The heart can be sacrificed on an [[Aranei shrine]] to restore 50% special attack energy and up to 24 prayer points, useful to extend trip length. Another potential way to extend trips is to utilise either the [[Saradomin godsword]] or [[Ancient godsword]] special attack. Despite these two weapons not being [[vampyrebane weapons]], their special attacks still work as if you had hit. A [[garlic cocktail]] in one's inventory will not make them aggressive.

Venators were bred by the vampyres to be used for blood sport and hunting.{{CiteNews|url=https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/the-blood-moon-rises---overview-?oldschool=1|title=The Blood Moon Rises - Overview|newsdate=25 January 2026|quote=Among Vampyrium’s deadliest inhabitants are the Venators - vampyric pack beasts bred for blood sport and relentless pursuit.}} They are believed to be the closest living relative to vampyres.{{CiteNPC|npc=Aranei scout|quote=Father Sugadinti believes they [venators] are the closest living relative to vampyres, making them very useful indeed.}}

